<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mingyi Nyo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1459–<a href="/years/1530">1530</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mingyi Nyo was the founder of the Toungoo dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, ruler of the small principality of Toungoo on the Sittaung river from 1485. As the kingdom of Ava weakened, he declared independence in 1510 and built Toungoo into a refuge for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamar-people">Burmans</a> fleeing Shan raids in the north. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabinshwehti">Tabinshwehti</a> and Tabinshwehti's brother-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayinnaung">Bayinnaung</a> built on this base to create the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-toungoo-empire">First Toungoo Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mingyi-nyo.jpg" alt="Mingyi Nyo" width="207" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tawoo / Tawoo at en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mingyi_Nyo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Toungoo, a small Burmese principality on the Sittaung river, grew in strength under <b>Mingyi Nyo</b>, who declared independence from Ava in 1510.</blockquote><a href="/state/first-toungoo-empire">First Toungoo Empire</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Inwa, in what is now <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a>. Died in Taungoo, in what is now <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=21.86,95.99&amp;year=1505" aria-label="Inwa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7124 1356 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Mingyi Nyo"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7574 1626h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7574 1626h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=21.86,95.99&amp;year=1505">What was here in 1505? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
